.Dd September 16, 2026
.Dt NDI_DEVI_FINDCHILD 9F
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ndi_devi_findchild ,
.Nm ndi_devi_find ,
.Nm ndi_devi_findchild_by_callback
.Nd find an immediate child device node
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/sunndi.h
.Ft "dev_info_t *"
.Fo ndi_devi_findchild
.Fa "dev_info_t *p"
.Fa "char *devname"
.Fc
.Ft "dev_info_t *"
.Fo ndi_devi_find
.Fa "dev_info_t *p"
.Fa "char *cname"
.Fa "char *caddr"
.Fc
.Ft "dev_info_t *"
.Fo ndi_devi_findchild_by_callback
.Fa "dev_info_t *p"
.Fa "char *dname"
.Fa "char *ua"
.Fa "int (*make_ua)(dev_info_t *, char *, int)"
.Fc
.Sh INTERFACE LEVEL
illumos specific
.Pq Consolidation Private .
.Sh PARAMETERS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Va p
Parent nexus to search.
.It Va devname
Null-terminated child name, normally \fBname@address\fP.
.It Va cname , caddr
Separate node name and unit address for the older interface.
.It Va dname , ua
Driver name, or \fBNULL\fP for any driver, and unit address to match.
.It Va make_ua
Callback that obtains an address for an unnamed child.
.El
.Sh DESCRIPTION
\fBndi_devi_findchild()\fP searches the immediate children of \fBp\fP for a node whose
node name and unit address match \fBdevname\fP.
Children that have no unit address are skipped.
The caller must own the parent's critical section using \fBndi_devi_enter()\fP.
The search does not enumerate or attach children.
.Pp
\fBndi_devi_find()\fP is the older interface taking the name and address
separately.
It enters and exits the parent's critical section internally.
New callers should use \fBndi_devi_findchild()\fP and explicitly protect the
result's lifetime.
.Pp
\fBndi_devi_findchild_by_callback()\fP matches the driver binding selected by
\fBdname\fP and the unit address \fBua\fP.
If \fBdname\fP is \fBNULL\fP, it matches by address alone.
For a child with no address, it calls \fBmake_ua(child, buffer, length)\fP.
The callback must write a null-terminated unit address within the supplied
buffer and return \fBDDI_SUCCESS\fP, or return \fBDDI_FAILURE\fP to skip the child.
The temporary address is used only for comparison and is not assigned to the
child.
The caller must own the parent's critical section.
.Pp
None of these functions takes a reference on the result.
Before leaving the parent's critical section, call \fBndi_hold_devi()\fP if the
pointer must remain valid afterwards.
.Sh CONTEXT
These functions may be called from user or kernel context.
They may sleep.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
These functions return the matching device node, or \fBNULL\fP if no
matching child is found.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ndi_devi_enter 9F ,
.Xr ndi_hold_devi 9F ,
.Xr ndi_merge_node 9F ,
.Xr sunndi 9F
